  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Preliminary 0.3.0 release. BREAKING: ITableFileSystem.RenameAsync is removed and replaced by TryWriteAllBytesAsync, which creates a file only if it does not already exist; any custom ITableFileSystem must implement it, and it must be atomic, because table-format commit protocols depend on exactly one writer creating a given version. Delta Lake commits now cost a single conditional request per commit instead of a write-to-temp plus rename. New: DeltaTable.CreateOrReplaceAsync publishes protocol, metadata, removes and initial data in one commit, creating a table with data or atomically replacing an existing one while preserving its history. The Google Cloud Storage backend moves to Clast.Google.Cloud.Storage.V1 4.15.0. EngineeredWood is pre-1.0: every public API is subject to change — without notice and without a deprecation cycle — until 1.0.0. Pin an exact version if you depend on a package.",
